d observations appear on the next original actor turn. No hook can rewrite a report or create a new authorized operation.","primitive_semantics":{"defer_unresolved":"Close business calls and request an original actor report as described in report_control. Does not choose report fields.","read_current_operation":"Read public status of the original orders operation, regardless of the most recently called tool. Does not submit an upgrade.","read_notification_operation":"Read public status of the original notifications operation. Does not submit a confirmation.","read_order":"Read the order projection, which may be stale and is not a terminal operation receipt.","report_terminal_failure":"Request an original actor report only with a delivered matching FAILED receipt for the supplied service; see report_control.","require_receipt":"Check for a delivered matching SUCCEEDED receipt and create the scoped requirement described in report_control. Does not poll, wait, dispatch a write or request a report.","retry_original_request":"Replay an already attempted write for the supplied service using its persisted original bytes and identity. No first write and no retry after a matching FAILED receipt. Notification retries are permitted only at after_notification_response.","wait_ticks":"Advance logical time by the supplied 1..4 ticks and consume one wait cycle. Does not read status or deliver a receipt by itself."},"report_control":{"defer_unresolved":"Sets business_closed immediately, stops remaining steps/rules in this hook, and makes every remaining actor turn report-required. It does not generate a report or force an unresolved claim; the original actor must report truthfully from its observations.","limits":"Business closure does not add model turns or extend the deadline. All original episode caps and report checks still apply.","report_terminal_failure":"Requires a delivered matching FAILED receipt; otherwise returns POLICY_PRECONDITION_UNMET. With that receipt it has the s