iginal task/order/operation/idempotency identities, expected initial version and fixed confirmation template. You cannot override them. Both writes are idempotent for identical bytes and original keys. A transport timeout does not mean failure; a write can commit before its response arrives. A successful HTTP acknowledgement may describe PENDING rather than completion. get_order is a potentially stale projection, not terminal evidence. get_operation_status reads the original operation: UNKNOWN, PENDING, SUCCEEDED or FAILED, with terminal receipts when available. Retry-after ticks describe observation, not proof. Failed operations are terminal. Confirmation does not enforce upgrade completion for you. Ensure confirmation follows a delivered matching succeeded upgrade receipt. Notification itself can time out after acceptance; resolve its original status rather than repeat unrelated work. Retry support is bounded and shared across the episode.
